[h1]Phobos Exchange 0.5.2[/h1]
[b]Draft - not published | 2026-10-08[/b]

[h2]Fixed[/h2]

[list]
[*]Share prices could be steered by dumping cargo on a station. Each company follows a few stations' cargo markets, and the price factor the game shows there moves with how full the station's stores are, which any player can change by selling it a hold of the cheapest goods in a category: a few hundred credits of drink bottles or medicine boxes could swing a company's price by a third. Companies now follow what those stations need, recovered from the game's factor and its stock, so filling or emptying a station's stores no longer moves a share price. Blockades, the stations' production and the game's own events still do (owner decision, 8 October 2026).
[/list]

[h2]Changed[/h2]

[list]
[*]The market wire now says a price moved as demand rose or eased at a station, instead of as goods ran short or piled up there. The drivers readout in the F3 console shows the factor the station's demand gives at half stock.
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility and limits[/h2]

[list]
[*]Saves: a market from an earlier version opens at its saved prices; its station signals settle once to the new reading, so nothing jumps. The save then notes that it follows demand.
[*]Checked offline; not yet seen in the game.
[/list]
